{"seq":39,"ts":"2026-08-26T09:08:51.649Z","type":"work.add","payload":{"id":"tsk-2jg","title":"Bug in fgos approve/assertPlanEvidence for a heavy-risk work item that was never individually…","description":"Bug in fgos approve/assertPlanEvidence for a heavy-risk work item that was never individually claimed/branched (its work landed via a parent's own single-commit implementation instead of a per-child dispatch cycle -- confirmed live on tsk-28x-1..12, docs/history/tsk-28x/plan.md exists and covers every child's own phase but under the parent's docs-history dir, not the child's own). Two coupled problems found while retroactively syncing tsk-28x's 12 children to reality after their code was verified already on main: (1) assertPlanEvidence (src/state/store.mjs:621) unconditionally does 'git cat-file -e fgw/<id>:<path>' to find a heavy-risk item's plan.md -- for an item that never had its own fgw/<id> branch (this exact 'child absorbed into parent' shape, or any item pull-doored via take/return per docs/how-to/close-out-a-work-item-already-done-before-claim.md), there is structurally no branch to check, so a heavy-risk item can never reach 'delivered' through the documented pull-door path even though docsRef can point at a real, existing plan.md. (2) classifySource (src/runner/merge.mjs:236) checks branchExists(fgw/<id>) FIRST, before headAtTake/headAtReturn -- so creating a compensating fgw/<id> branch purely to satisfy assertPlanEvidence's git-cat-file check flips classification from pull/legacy to 'runner', which then drags the item into the full leaf-into-root git merge machinery (mergeRunnerItem, withMergeEphemeralWorktree) instead of the lightweight pull-door verify-only path. Reproduced live: creating fgw/tsk-28x-1 at current main tip (to satisfy the plan.md gate) made approve try to merge it into the parent's own fgw/tsk-28x branch, which is STALE (untouched since tsk-28x's own merge into main days ago) -- the diff against that stale branch pulled in every .fgos/ event file that has landed on main since, tripping the ADR0020 fgos-write-rejected guard (no .fgos/ mutation via a leaf merge) and parking the item 'blocked'. Net effect: a heavy-risk item that is retroactively synced (take -> return --no-new-commits-ok, code already on main, no real branch ever existed) has no working path to 'delivered' today -- it can reach awaiting-approval (return succeeds) but approve is a dead end (assertPlanEvidence fails with no branch; creating a branch to pass that check breaks the merge classification instead). Needs a design fix, likely one of: assertPlanEvidence should also accept a docsRef-resolved path checked against the CURRENT working tree/main when no fgw/<id> branch exists and classifySource resolves the item as pull/legacy (mirroring how the pull-door verify-only path in approve.mjs already re-runs verify against the current tree rather than a branch); or classifySource should not reclassify to 'runner' purely because a same-named branch happens to exist if the item's own recorded claim source was pull/legacy. Workaround used this session: left the 12 tsk-28x children parked at awaiting-approval (real, re-verified, not a fabricated status) rather than forcing them further through the broken approve path.","kind":"bug","status":"todo","deps":[],"risk":"light","refs":[],"verify":"chưa xác định — P15 bổ sung","tier":"light","mode":"sync","domain":"coding","stage":"discovery","statusCategory":"todo"},"v":3,"src":"2c65ef08-839f-49cf-8a6e-ef293ee060f4","h":"7e52ec25594b48a1"}
